# Per-machine and per-person, never shared. `settings.json` beside it is the workspace's
# settings and is tracked; this one is whatever the person at this desk allowed today, and
# committing it would apply one machine's answers to everybody else's.
#
# This is the whole reason the two files have different names. Claude Code reads both and
# merges them, local winning, so the split is already the tool's -- it is only the tracking
# decision that is ours.
settings.local.json
.DS_Store
__pycache__

# The plugins are their own repository now -- fire/agent-plugins, private, checked out here
# at the path Claude Code reads. Two different kinds of thing were in one repository: this
# one is settings and permissions, reviewed by everyone who works here, and that one is code
# with a memory store in it recording what an agent has learned about the work.
#
# A nested checkout is untracked from this repository's point of view, and `repo` permits the
# nesting -- _CheckLocalPath validates a path in isolation and has no overlap rule. Ignoring
# it is what keeps `git status` here answering about the configuration rather than reporting
# somebody else's repository as a pile of new files.
plugins/
